From carrier population to measured current (@mat-charge-transport: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @materials-engineering, #source "../sources/Solid-State-Physics-Tong.lingua#r_2G2CQ9C5QDEBTQ2YNMYQ5QK3MB", #source "../sources/Solid-State-Physics-Simon-2012.lingua#r_3R4Q71S31MD0EH6YVDQQ2ESKH5", #source "../sources/Functional-Materials-MIT-3-23.lingua#r_3TPN5CK13R844S7PGFK7C1STVN", #materials-engineering "../../../physics/electromagnetism/currents/Drift-diffusion-relaxation-and-Ohm-law.lingua#r_3P3417NJ3B753K217S24RZY08D") { r_087VW2TPEQP1NFNM75PYPY4M0W
**Read:** [Solid State Physics — David Tong](../sources/Solid-State-Physics-Tong.lingua#r_2G2CQ9C5QDEBTQ2YNMYQ5QK3MB), chapter 3; [Solid State Physics — Steven H. Simon, 2012 draft](../sources/Solid-State-Physics-Simon-2012.lingua#r_3R4Q71S31MD0EH6YVDQQ2ESKH5), chapters 3–4 and 16–17; [Electrical, Optical, and Magnetic Properties of Materials — MIT 3.23](../sources/Functional-Materials-MIT-3-23.lingua#r_3TPN5CK13R844S7PGFK7C1STVN), transport; the following shared electromagnetic current and Hall Records.

For independent dilute electron and hole populations, σ=e(nμ_n+pμ_p), where mobility μ_n or μ_p is distinct from chemical potential μ. A measured resistance also contains geometry and contacts. Temperature can increase the number of carriers while reducing mobility; the net trend is not determined by either effect alone.

For n=10²² m⁻³ and electron mobility 0.1 m² V⁻¹ s⁻¹ with negligible holes, σ≈160.2177 S m⁻¹. This is an illustrative input, not a grade specification. A one-carrier Hall interpretation can fail for mixed carriers, anisotropy or nontrivial scattering.

**Work:** Derive a drift/diffusion balance, follow both shared Records and reconstruct a measured conductivity/Hall pair. Infer which combinations of parameters the data determine. Compare a changed-temperature prediction with evidence before assigning a unique microscopic mechanism.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
